- op: discuss  # ecef
  at: '2026-06-07T06:35:44Z'  # ecef
  by: agent  # ecef
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ecef
  clock: 2  # ecef
  nonce: ecef  # ecef
  message: "Dogfood finding (member F141.A2-b, split from F141.A2), reproduces on the frozen substrate. Mechanism: the JS module linker synthesizes package nodes for npm dependencies but leaves the top-level path field empty (path=\"\"), encoding the package name only in the id (typescript:npm:0-0:<name>:npm_package) and leaving language=null with an all-zero span. Scope: exactly 2 nodes — typescript:npm:0-0:lit:npm_package and typescript:npm:0-0:vite:npm_package, kind=package, origin=js-module-linker, path=\"\". These are the only empty-path nodes in the substrate. Exposure: a consumer joining package nodes on node.path to a manifest or directory, or filtering nodes by path, drops or mis-buckets these dependency nodes; an agent building a dependency inventory keyed on path silently omits the affected npm packages. Expectation: either path carries a meaningful locator (the manifest or package directory) or the field is documented as intentionally empty for synthetic dependency nodes. Sibling of WI-kapul (external_symbol path=\"<external>\" vs id path-slot); split because the producer (js-module-linker) and the empty-string sentinel differ from the <external> placeholder case. Substrate evidence: probe_1_emptypath.log."  # ecef
- op: discuss  # 8496
  at: '2026-09-25T17:44:57Z'  # 8496
  by: agent  # 8496
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8496
  clock: 3  # 8496
  nonce: '8496'  # 8496
  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). STILL REPRODUCES, but narrower than filed. Status unchanged.\n\nFixture: a.ts importing from \"lit\"; full survey. Emitted node:\n  id=typescript:npm:0-0:lit:package, kind=package, path=\"\", language=null, discovery_language=typescript, span 0-0.\nThe same survey also has one `<external>` node, so a single artifact now carries TWO no-anchor spellings of node.path: \"\" and \"<external>\".\n\nWhat changed since filing (06-07):\n- language=null and the all-zero span are BY DESIGN now:\n  - linkers/js_module.py:876-897 marks the node as an ADR-0031 Class B synthetic, with discovery_language carrying the context;\n  - span 0-0 is ADR-0036 Ruling 3's \"synthetic node with no source location\" sentinel.\n  Those two parts of the title are not defects.\n- The kind is now `package` (the id's kind slot says package, not npm_package).\n- Since 1c2ce91f7b (06-15) the producer COMMENTS in favour of path=\"\": \"no declaring manifest path, so path=\\\"\\\" keeps it a single logical node (ADR-0035 §4 ...)\".\n\nThe live question: WI-kapul was closed wont_do on 07-22 on the ruling that node.path is the filesystem anchor, with the documented `<external>` sentinel for \"no file anchor\" (ADR-0036 Ruling 3 table). An npm stand-in has no file anchor either, yet it uses an UNDECLARED \"\" instead of the declared sentinel. So either \"\" joins the enumeration with its own meaning, or this node takes `<external>`. That is a decision. Recommend re-titling to \"npm_package stand-in uses path=\\\"\\\" where the declared no-anchor sentinel is <external>\"."  # 8496
